From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:51:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] meshcore: keep MeshCore messages out of the Meshtastic
 conversation list

The two protocols stay in their own apps. This tab does not translate nodes or messages across them.

diff --git a/feature/meshcore/README.md b/feature/meshcore/README.md
index c0a70cb1b6930fde6ed78e9094321b46edd7ab5b..311df0a9c64bb822fd1f69a584d4c402081d9b34 100644
--- a/feature/meshcore/README.md
+++ b/feature/meshcore/README.md
@@ -52,8 +52,8 @@ channel or contact opens a chat pane with a message composer.
   firmware series. Use Meshtastic over Bluetooth while this tab uses USB: the
   phone can claim that serial port only once, and the Meshtastic service reads
   every byte on it.
-- The app does not bridge MeshCore messages into the Meshtastic conversations
-  list. That requires the optional bridge described in the raumata design docs.
+- MeshCore messages stay in this tab. They are not copied into the Meshtastic
+  conversation list, and Meshtastic nodes are not shown as MeshCore contacts.
 - Only the companion subset implemented by the firmware is available: app
   start, device query, contacts, channels, text, adverts and battery/storage.
 - The USB transport is Android-only; desktop uses the no-op adapter until a
